#              with --features all)
# Invocation:  wasmtime run host-resource-reuse.wasm
# Engine:      wasmtime 49.0.3 (f96eabaa1 2026-10-14), darwin/arm64.
#
# reader                                      reading
# wasmtime 49.0.3, 10 of 10                   1 1 2
# Burroughs at 7321e3d, 3 of 3                1 2 3
# Burroughs with ADR 0117's build             1 1 2
#
# Meaning:     the three indices get-stdout returned, printed one per line. The second call follows a drop of the
#              first handle, so the reference's Table reuses its slot (def:Table.add pops the free list); the
#              third follows no drop, so it takes the next slot. Burroughs minted from a counter on the Host that
#              never reused a number, because every resource.drop was a no-op: 1 2 3.
